  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5353",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to ASPC1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets ASPC1. This indicates a direct or indirect relationship between Mollicellin N and ASPC1, mediated by the intermediate compound 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. The presence of multiple pathways converging on this central molecule supports a robust mechanism where Mollicellin N may influence ASPC1 through a shared target. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating ASPC1 activity, possibly through a broader regulatory network. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a well-defined relationship that is supported by multiple layers of molecular interaction.",
